      "opacity": 100,
      "seed": 15083,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 61877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MENTAL MODEL: Escape analysis is like asking 'does this variable need to survive after the function returns?'\n   If YES -> heap (GC managed). If NO -> stack (free! no GC). The compiler is conservative when unsure.\nZERO-ALLOC: return value semantics (not pointers), use sync.Pool for reuse, avoid interface boxing in hot loops",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MENTAL MODEL: Escape analysis is like asking 'does this variable need to survive after the function returns?'\n   If YES -> heap (GC managed). If NO -> stack (free! no GC). The compiler is conservative when unsure.\nZERO-ALLOC: return value semantics (not pointers), use sync.Pool for reuse, avoid interface boxing in hot loops",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
